00:54:46.380 --> 00:54:47.880
I just love this picture of her.

1254
00:54:48.080 --> 00:54:49.040
I'll put it in our stories.

1255
00:54:49.560 --> 00:54:52.000
Well, around this time, Daryl's had enough.

1256
00:54:52.160 --> 00:54:53.320
He's going to get in the water.

1257
00:54:53.500 --> 00:54:58.520
He decides being with Val is more important than worrying about what he looks like.

1258
00:54:58.520 --> 00:54:59.620
He takes off his shirt.

1259
00:54:59.620 --> 00:55:02.660
He does a big cannonball, and Val is totally delighted.

1260
00:55:03.180 --> 00:55:06.160
This is when Erin is going to swim up to Andy.

1261
00:55:06.540 --> 00:55:08.600
Guess what she found at the bottom of the pool?

1262
00:55:09.040 --> 00:55:10.200
The engagement ring.

1263
00:55:10.620 --> 00:55:14.920
And she knows that it's a family heirloom because it has the Bernard family seal on it.

1264
00:55:15.060 --> 00:55:18.920
And this is another way where Andy's like, oh, she really knows me.

1265
00:55:19.100 --> 00:55:19.680
She knows me.

1266
00:55:19.920 --> 00:55:20.280
Mm-hmm.

1267
00:55:20.920 --> 00:55:22.740
Well, Robert's tour is complete.

1268
00:55:23.120 --> 00:55:25.240
They've made it back to the pool area.

1269
00:55:25.500 --> 00:55:27.540
Jim is still trying to leave.

1270
00:55:27.540 --> 00:55:34.200
And this is when Robert is going to look around, and he is going to realize that this thing

1271
00:55:34.200 --> 00:55:38.120
that he's wanted to happen in his house all along is happening.

1272
00:55:38.640 --> 00:55:41.800
People are loose, and they're drinking, and they're laughing.

1273
00:55:42.380 --> 00:55:44.340
Oscar is Bacchus, god of wine.

1274
00:55:44.580 --> 00:55:44.980
Yes.

1275
00:55:45.560 --> 00:55:50.860
Well, during the montage when Robert's looking around, if you were also curious why Creed

1276
00:55:50.860 --> 00:55:55.560
is laying on the ground playing the guitar in a black Speedo wearing a gold crown, I

1277
00:55:55.560 --> 00:55:56.400
was right there with you.

1278
00:55:56.720 --> 00:55:58.080
I did not notice this.

1279
00:55:58.260 --> 00:56:01.580
You didn't see Creed wearing a gold crown on his head?

1280
00:56:01.660 --> 00:56:03.660
No, we didn't get any mail about it either.

1281
00:56:04.380 --> 00:56:05.180
Come on.

1282
00:56:05.640 --> 00:56:06.660
Not that I saw.

1283
00:56:06.800 --> 00:56:07.100
Okay.

1284
00:56:07.340 --> 00:56:08.940
Well, I was incredibly curious.

1285
00:56:08.940 --> 00:56:11.100
I was like, why does Creed have a gold crown?

1286
00:56:11.260 --> 00:56:12.080
Where did this come from?

1287
00:56:12.220 --> 00:56:14.820
I went to the shooting draft, and there was a deleted scene.

1288
00:56:15.560 --> 00:56:15.960
What?

1289
00:56:15.960 --> 00:56:19.020
It said, interior Robert's bedroom.

1290
00:56:19.640 --> 00:56:21.800
Creed cracks open Robert's safe.

1291
00:56:21.960 --> 00:56:25.460
He finds a velvet box and carefully opens it.

1292
00:56:25.960 --> 00:56:27.380
Inside is a crown.

1293
00:56:27.800 --> 00:56:29.620
Creed says the following.

1294
00:56:30.140 --> 00:56:32.020
Ah, here it is.

1295
00:56:32.260 --> 00:56:36.380
Creed takes out a pocket knife and begins to pry a diamond from the crown.

1296
00:56:36.740 --> 00:56:39.620
He took the diamond out and, though, also kept the crown.

1297
00:56:39.860 --> 00:56:44.660
And wore it in front of Robert, so Robert would have known immediately that he cracked open

1298
00:56:44.660 --> 00:56:45.200
his safe.

1299
00:56:45.840 --> 00:56:48.520
Also, why does Robert have an elaborate gold crown?

1300
00:56:48.820 --> 00:56:50.160
That was not explained.

1301
00:56:50.400 --> 00:56:52.280
Maybe that's part of his generational wealth.

1302
00:56:53.000 --> 00:56:53.480
Hmm.

1303
00:56:53.980 --> 00:56:54.940
Supports your theory.

1304
00:56:55.080 --> 00:56:55.680
Yes, it does.

1305
00:56:56.220 --> 00:57:00.200
Well, Robert's going to be so excited by what he sees, he's going to take off all of his

1306
00:57:00.200 --> 00:57:03.860
clothes in front of all of his employees, and he's going to go swimming.

1307
00:57:05.040 --> 00:57:06.360
Backstroke, no less.

1308
00:57:06.560 --> 00:57:10.140
Yes, that was specifically noted in the script that he does a backstroke.

1309
00:57:10.420 --> 00:57:14.920
Was there anything from Standards and Practices about the blurred of the crotch area?

1310
00:57:15.200 --> 00:57:16.300
Oh, yes, lady.

1311
00:57:16.560 --> 00:57:17.740
There sure was.

1312
00:57:17.900 --> 00:57:22.000
Steve Burgess gets his first, as previously noted.

1313
00:57:22.280 --> 00:57:22.620
Oh!

1314
00:57:23.680 --> 00:57:28.900
Because, you know, Ryan and Gabe also get undressed and get into the pool.

1315
00:57:29.430 --> 00:57:32.720
And, of course, you all know, they were not actually naked.

1316
00:57:33.020 --> 00:57:34.060
No one was naked.

1317
00:57:34.520 --> 00:57:35.580
No, they were wearing nude shorts.

1318
00:57:35.720 --> 00:57:39.860
However, Steve Burgess said they all had to sign nudity waivers, nonetheless.

1319
00:57:39.860 --> 00:57:45.040
But Steve said, we also got this note from Standards and Practices.

1320
00:57:45.440 --> 00:57:49.980
As previously noted, please blur all nudity here and throughout.

1321
00:57:50.320 --> 00:57:52.340
Nothing should be visible through the effect.

1322
00:57:52.920 --> 00:57:55.020
That was their note on the scene.

1323
00:57:55.360 --> 00:57:55.600
Okay.

1324
00:57:55.600 --> 00:58:01.480
I did laugh really hard at how Gabe just falls in with his pants half on his feet.

1325
00:58:02.280 --> 00:58:03.720
You know who else loved that?

1326
00:58:03.840 --> 00:58:05.760
Was Rachel Kaye from Denton, Texas.

1327
00:58:06.400 --> 00:58:07.160
You know what?

1328
00:58:07.280 --> 00:58:08.260
That was not scripted.

1329
00:58:09.700 --> 00:58:11.380
Zach couldn't get his pants off.

1330
00:58:11.680 --> 00:58:16.680
Steve Burgess said that he improvised that, and everyone kind of freaked out because they're

1331
00:58:16.680 --> 00:58:20.940
like, is he going to be able to swim with his legs bound up like that?

1332
00:58:20.940 --> 00:58:23.420
But it worked, and that's the take we used.

1333
00:58:23.480 --> 00:58:24.280
It's really funny.

1334
00:58:24.840 --> 00:58:26.840
Well, that pretty much wraps up pool party.

1335
00:58:26.940 --> 00:58:28.800
No one really wanted to hang around after that.

1336
00:58:29.100 --> 00:58:29.700
That's right.

1337
00:58:29.840 --> 00:58:33.420
I mean, Jim drove over some bushes to finally go home.

1338
00:58:33.460 --> 00:58:34.900
He was like, get me the hell out of here.

1339
00:58:35.160 --> 00:58:38.520
Well, we did have one final fan question from Haley M.

1340
00:58:38.700 --> 00:58:40.540
in Shawnee, Oklahoma, who said,

1341
00:58:40.660 --> 00:58:44.080
did the cast get to have a pool party behind the scenes?

1342
00:58:44.780 --> 00:58:47.100
Because that sounds like it could be a lot of fun.

1343
00:58:47.960 --> 00:58:52.960
I wasn't there, Haley, but Angela, I'm imagining that when you wrapped, you all were very happy

1344
00:58:52.960 --> 00:58:54.220
to get away from the pool.

1345
00:58:54.640 --> 00:58:55.980
We were done.

1346
00:58:56.280 --> 00:58:56.580
Yeah.

1347
00:58:56.580 --> 00:58:58.240
You were like, we've been in the pool all day.

1348
00:58:58.480 --> 00:58:59.200
We're out.

1349
00:58:59.840 --> 00:59:04.720
There was, however, something going on during the shooting of this episode that was quite

1350
00:59:04.720 --> 00:59:09.160
fun, which is that the St. Louis Cardinals were in the World Series.

1351
00:59:09.500 --> 00:59:15.420
And as you know, we had a lot of St. Louis folks on our crew and in our cast, and Ellie

1352
00:59:15.420 --> 00:59:16.840
Kemper sent in a clip about it.

1353
00:59:17.580 --> 00:59:22.520
Jenna, I remember the St. Louis Cardinals were in the World Series at the time.

1354
00:59:22.680 --> 00:59:27.480
I had this memory of them being in the World Series, and Phyllis kept sneaking out to the

1355
00:59:27.480 --> 00:59:30.280
van to listen to the game on the radio.

1356
00:59:30.580 --> 00:59:33.300
So go St. Louis, go pool party.

1357
00:59:33.640 --> 00:59:34.040
Okay.

1358
00:59:34.880 --> 00:59:37.560
That's all my deep thoughts about pool party.

1359
00:59:37.720 --> 00:59:38.240
Thanks, ladies.

1360
00:59:39.460 --> 00:59:44.580
Well, Steve Burgess said that in addition to having the game on inside the vans, they also

1361
00:59:44.580 --> 00:59:46.220
had it on a TV outside.

1362
00:59:47.480 --> 00:59:49.320
Lady, this game was huge.

1363
00:59:49.640 --> 00:59:54.640
This was the St. Louis Cardinals versus the Texas Rangers.

1364
00:59:55.100 --> 00:59:56.820
And you know, Lee is from Texas.

1365
00:59:57.200 --> 00:59:57.480
Yes.

1366
00:59:57.760 --> 00:59:59.060
Well, my son was one month old.

1367
00:59:59.060 --> 01:00:00.620
My sister came out to visit.

1368
01:00:00.840 --> 01:00:03.720
She brought all kinds of Cardinals gear for my son to wear.

1369
01:00:03.960 --> 01:00:09.560
And Lee and I had an agreement where we either had to alternate the St. Louis Cardinals onesie

1370
01:00:09.560 --> 01:00:13.640
and the Texas Rangers onesie, or he had to wear a little bit of each team.

1371
01:00:14.600 --> 01:00:15.080
Aw.

1372
01:00:15.080 --> 01:00:15.200
Aw.

1373
01:00:15.480 --> 01:00:20.300
So listen, game six of that World Series is epic because of David Freese.

1374
01:00:20.480 --> 01:00:22.740
I won't go on and on, but oh my gosh.

1375
01:00:22.860 --> 01:00:28.540
First of all, he ties it up, and then he has a walk-off homer in the 11th inning for them

1376
01:00:28.540 --> 01:00:31.920
to win that game, which they needed to win in order to get to the seventh game.

1377
01:00:32.560 --> 01:00:39.100
For the seventh game of the World Series, I sneaked two Cardinals socks on my son's feet.

1378
01:00:39.220 --> 01:00:40.300
And the Cardinals won!

1379
01:00:40.300 --> 01:00:41.640
And I think that's why.

1380
01:00:43.680 --> 01:00:45.280
I love Arlington Stadium.

1381
01:00:45.300 --> 01:00:46.880
We would go there and watch ballgames.

1382
01:00:47.000 --> 01:00:47.500
It's beautiful.

1383
01:00:47.700 --> 01:00:49.400
You're making me want to go to a baseball game.

1384
01:00:49.540 --> 01:00:50.000
I know.

1385
01:00:50.500 --> 01:00:51.780
Well, listen, everybody.

1386
01:00:52.040 --> 01:00:53.340
That was pool party.

1387
01:00:53.520 --> 01:00:59.940
But before we leave, I think we need to have a birthday party.

1388
01:01:00.360 --> 01:01:00.840
What?

1389
01:01:01.280 --> 01:01:07.120
Because, Angela Kinsey, we are recording this episode right before we go on our summer break.

1390
01:01:07.220 --> 01:01:09.300
Your birthday is June 25th.

1391
01:01:09.300 --> 01:01:11.980
And we're going to be on vacation for your birthday.

1392
01:01:12.800 --> 01:01:16.320
I hope I did a good job as party coordinator this time.

1393
01:01:16.480 --> 01:01:18.220
I can't believe you remembered this.

1394
01:01:18.300 --> 01:01:21.640
I also can't believe I almost forgot to pick you up this morning.

1395
01:01:21.840 --> 01:01:22.380
I know.

1396
01:01:22.840 --> 01:01:24.460
I've been driving Jenna to work.

1397
01:01:24.560 --> 01:01:25.300
We've been carpooling.

1398
01:01:25.380 --> 01:01:26.300
It's been so fun.

1399
01:01:26.320 --> 01:01:28.540
I've really enjoyed it because of my broken shoulder.

1400
01:01:28.760 --> 01:01:33.020
And this morning I was on autopilot, and I just got on the freeway and went the wrong way.

1401
01:01:33.660 --> 01:01:35.300
I was so worried.

1402
01:01:35.300 --> 01:01:37.160
How am I going to hide the birthday stuff?

1403
01:01:37.400 --> 01:01:39.040
Because you're driving me to work.

1404
01:01:39.040 --> 01:01:40.880
So that's why I had a giant bag with me today.

1405
01:01:41.020 --> 01:01:41.700
You didn't ask.

1406
01:01:41.880 --> 01:01:42.340
Thank goodness.

1407
01:01:42.780 --> 01:01:44.280
Here's your present, Ange.

1408
01:01:44.380 --> 01:01:45.420
You're so sweet.

1409
01:01:45.420 --> 01:01:46.540
I can't believe this.

1410
01:01:46.640 --> 01:01:47.600
This is so cute.

1411
01:01:48.480 --> 01:01:49.300
Oh, my gosh.

1412
01:01:49.400 --> 01:01:51.480
I didn't do my hair or anything today.

1413
01:01:51.480 --> 01:01:51.540
I know.

1414
01:01:51.620 --> 01:01:52.260
I thought of that.

1415
01:01:52.340 --> 01:01:53.940
You said I didn't have time to get ready.

1416
01:01:54.100 --> 01:01:55.580
I'm going to show up in my pajamas.

1417
01:01:55.580 --> 01:01:58.380
And I was like, well, we might be taking some pictures.

1418
01:01:58.520 --> 01:01:59.680
You got me a succulent?

1419
01:02:00.020 --> 01:02:00.460
Of course.

1420
01:02:00.620 --> 01:02:01.060
Aw.

1421
01:02:01.380 --> 01:02:01.720
Wait.

1422
01:02:01.880 --> 01:02:03.020
I got to fish it out.

1423
01:02:03.320 --> 01:02:07.860
I didn't get you any, like, birthday sweet treat because I know Josh does that.

1424
01:02:07.940 --> 01:02:09.320
You have plenty of sweet treats.

1425
01:02:09.500 --> 01:02:10.460
Oh, the pen is mine.

1426
01:02:10.760 --> 01:02:11.240
Sorry.

1427
01:02:14.100 --> 01:02:16.180
Oh, this is so cute.

1428
01:02:16.220 --> 01:02:17.880
I love a succulent.

1429
01:02:18.460 --> 01:02:19.720
And you got me something.

1430
01:02:19.980 --> 01:02:21.720
You got me a little piece of...

1431
01:02:21.720 --> 01:02:22.980
What is it?

1432
01:02:23.880 --> 01:02:24.840
You guys.

1433
01:02:25.580 --> 01:02:27.340
It's a hummingbird necklace.

1434
01:02:27.760 --> 01:02:29.860
It's a little gold hummingbird.

1435
01:02:30.100 --> 01:02:32.680
It is so freaking cute.

1436
01:02:32.680 --> 01:02:34.520
I love it so much.

1437
01:02:34.520 --> 01:02:35.960
I'm putting it on right now.

1438
01:02:36.300 --> 01:02:37.720
Hummingbirds and succulents.

1439
01:02:37.960 --> 01:02:38.920
Equal Angela.

1440
01:02:39.180 --> 01:02:40.960
And we've got a card out there for you, too.

1441
01:02:41.140 --> 01:02:42.100
Everyone signed it.

1442
01:02:42.400 --> 01:02:42.620
Oh, my gosh.

1443
01:02:42.620 --> 01:02:43.640
I love it.

1444
01:02:43.800 --> 01:02:44.760
Thank you, guys.

1445
01:02:45.260 --> 01:02:45.560
Aw.

1446
01:02:45.760 --> 01:02:46.940
Happy birthday, Angela.

1447
01:02:47.220 --> 01:02:48.340
Happy pool party.

1448
01:02:48.700 --> 01:02:51.700
Thank you, Steve Burgess and Ellie Kemper and Amina.

1449
01:02:52.140 --> 01:02:55.560
And Matt Flynn and all of you guys for writing in with your questions.

1450
01:02:56.240 --> 01:02:57.520
We love you guys.

1451
01:02:57.740 --> 01:02:59.120
Oh, oh, lady, wait.

1452
01:02:59.220 --> 01:02:59.400
What?

1453
01:02:59.540 --> 01:03:01.160
One more thing before we go.

1454
01:03:01.700 --> 01:03:04.900
This episode is going to be airing in AuguSt.

1455
01:03:05.420 --> 01:03:05.820
August?

1456
01:03:06.360 --> 01:03:06.820
Yes.

1457
01:03:06.980 --> 01:03:12.900
So we should remind everyone about our live show that's going to be in Toronto on September

1458
01:03:12.900 --> 01:03:15.660
21st as part of the Just for Laughs Festival.

1459
01:03:15.900 --> 01:03:16.460
Oh, yes.

1460
01:03:16.460 --> 01:03:17.680
We are so excited.

1461
01:03:17.860 --> 01:03:18.640
So excited.

1462
01:03:18.640 --> 01:03:22.880
We had such a blast at Just for Laughs in Vancouver, and we can't wait to do it again.

1463
01:03:23.160 --> 01:03:23.500
Yes.

1464
01:03:23.600 --> 01:03:24.760
And tickets are still available.

1465
01:03:25.060 --> 01:03:27.220
I'll put a link in Office Ladies Pod Stories.

1466
01:03:27.600 --> 01:03:27.980
Great.

1467
01:03:28.260 --> 01:03:28.480
Okay.

1468
01:03:28.820 --> 01:03:30.100
Now we can go.

1469
01:03:30.360 --> 01:03:30.800
Bye.

1470
01:03:31.340 --> 01:03:31.720
Bye.

1471
